,"musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/9864b113-36d4-4076-9a1b-9b368f952315"},"photo":null,"bio":null},"Q24855768":{"id":"Q24855768","name":"Heize","ko":"헤이즈","birthName":"장다혜","birthNameEn":"","aliases":[],"birth":"1991-08-09","death":"","birthplace":"Daegu","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer","recording artist","singer-songwriter"],"debut":"2014","agencies":[{"name":"CJ ENM Entertainment Division","korean":true,"id":"Q10854462","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/heizeheize/","youtube":"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCsXigGjbC_l4ttk-oahTfVg","spotify":"https://open.spotify.com/artist/5dCvSnVduaFleCnyy98JMo","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/8cea34d9-e1a5-4a92-87da-de947f741fe6"},"photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/2e/Heize_at_Zion.T_X_Heize_Concert_on_April_21%2C_2018_%284%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Heize_at_Zion.T_X_Heize_Concert_on_April_21,_2018_(4)_(cropped).jpg","author":"seono의 BOL4 story","license":"CC BY 4.0"},"bio":{"text":"Jang Da-hye, better known by her stage name Heize (헤이즈), is a South Korean singer-songwriter, rapper, composer and producer currently signed to P Nation. The name Heize was inspired by the name of an American rapper Angel Haze, but instead of using the same English spelling, she decided to use Heize instead of Haze, because that was the spelling that came to mind. After making her debut in 2014 with the EP Heize, she gained attention after appearing on the second season of South Korean reality show Unpretty Rapstar. Shortly after, her breakout hit \"Star\" reached the top of the music charts.","title":"Heize","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heize"}},"Q28870936":{"id":"Q28870936","name":"Bona","ko":"보나","birthName":"김지연","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Kim Ji-yeon","Kim Jiyeon"],"birth":"1995-08-19","death":"","birthplace":"Daegu","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer","actor","model"],"debut":"2016","agencies":[{"name":"Starship Entertainment","korean":true,"id":"Q255363","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[{"id":"Q21964258","name":"WJSN","start":"","end":""},{"id":"Q108440398","name":"WJSN THE BLACK","start":"","end":""}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/bn_95819/","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/7ac83cfb-b7dd-42cb-ae5d-56c285676269"},"photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/78/190321_%EC%9A%B0%EC%A3%BC%EC%86%8C%EB%85%80_%EB%B3%B4%EB%82%98.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:190321_%EC%9A%B0%EC%A3%BC%EC%86%8C%EB%85%80_%EB%B3%B4%EB%82%98.jpg","author":"디스패치","license":"CC BY 3.0"},"bio":{"text":"Kim Ji-yeon, known professionally as Bona, is a South Korean singer and actress. She is a member of the South Korean girl group WJSN, and also its sub-unit WJSN The Black. She made her acting debut in the KBS2 drama Hit the Top (2017), and was cast as the female lead in the teen drama Girls' Generation 1979 (2018). Bona gained recognition for her portrayal as world champion and gold medalist fencer Ko Yu-rim in the tvN television series Twenty-Five Twenty-One (2022). Credited under her full name, she later starred in the television series Joseon Attorney (2023) and Pyramid Game (2024).","title":"Bona (singer)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bona_%28singer%29"}},"Q483288":{"id":"Q483288","name":"Nichkhun","ko":"닉쿤","birthName":"","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Nichkhun Buck Horvejkul"],"birth":"1988-06-24","death":"","birthplace":"Rancho Cucamonga","nationality":["United States","Thailand"],"height":null,"occupations":["rapper","singer","songwriter","dancer","actor"],"debut":"2008","agencies":[{"name":"JYP Entertainment","korean":true,"id":"Q483238","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[{"id":"Q222760","name":"2PM","start":"","end":""}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/khunsta0624/","x":"https://x.com/khunnie0624","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/f10a9097-d092-4d84-b8fd-30150412df66"},"photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/5b/Korean_Movie_%EA%B8%B0%EC%A0%81%EC%9D%98_%ED%94%BC%EC%95%84%EB%85%B8_The_Piano%2C_2015_%EB%8B%89%EC%BF%A4%EC%9D%98_%EC%9D%91%EC%9B%90_%EC%98%81%EC%83%81_Cheering_Video.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Korean_Movie_%EA%B8%B0%EC%A0%81%EC%9D%98_%ED%94%BC%EC%95%84%EB%85%B8_The_Piano,_2015_%EB%8B%89%EC%BF%A4%EC%9D%98_%EC%9D%91%EC%9B%90_%EC%98%81%EC%83%81_Cheering_Video.jpg","author":"JoinRunningMan","license":"CC BY 3.0"},"bio":{"text":"Nichkhun Buck Horvejkul, better known mononymously as Nichkhun, is a Thai and American singer-songwriter, rapper, and actor. Based in South Korea as a member of the South Korean boy band 2PM, Nichkhun is the first Southeast Asian individual to debut in a K-pop idol group. As a solo artist, Nichkhun has released two EPs. As an actor, he has starred in various Korean, Thai, and Chinese dramas and films such as Seven Something (2012), One and a Half Summer (2014), and Brother of the Year (2018). He has also worked as a television personality on several variety and reality programs such as We Got Married, We K-Pop, and Idol on Quiz.","title":"Nichkhun","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nichkhun"}},"Q488344":{"id":"Q488344","name":"Jang Wooyoung","ko":"우영","birthName":"장우영","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Wooyoung","Jang Woo-young"],"birth":"1989-04-30","death":"","birthplace":"Busan","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer","television actor","actor","film actor","recording artist"],"debut":"2008","agencies":[{"name":"JYP Entertainment","korean":true,"id":"Q483238","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[{"id":"Q222760","name":"2PM","start":"","end":""}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/dddnnnmm/","x":"https://x.com/0430yes","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/32ac762f-9d80-4dbc-a0c6-898de0592dac"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Jang Woo-young, known mononymously as Wooyoung, is a South Korean singer-songwriter and entertainer. In 2008, he debuted as a member of 2PM, a boy band currently managed by JYP Entertainment. He debuted as a solo artist in 2012 with his first extended play, 23, Male, Single. As of 2026, he has released a total of six EPs and one compilation album. Following his discharge from his mandatory military service in 2020, Jang has worked as a television personality on various Korean variety shows such as Beat Coin, I Can See Your Voice, and Street Man Fighter. He is also known for his role as Jason in the 2011 Korean drama Dream High.","title":"Jang Wooyoung","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jang_Wooyoung"}},"Q488600":{"id":"Q488600","name":"Moon Hee-joon","ko":"문희준","birthName":"","birthNameEn":"","aliases":[],"birth":"1978-03-14","death":"","birthplace":"Seoul","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer","actor","songwriter","record producer"],"debut":"1996","agencies":[{"name":"SM Entertainment","korean":true,"id":"Q483938","start":"","end":""},{"name":"IHQ","korean":true,"id":"Q7509507","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[{"id":"Q483135","name":"H.O.T.","start":"2018","end":"2019"}],"links":{"musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/45a133de-bece-43f8-833f-1605039e4732"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Moon Hee-jun is a South Korean pop rock singer-songwriter and dancer signed under SidusHQ. He initially rose to fame as the leader of former boy band H.O.T. under SM Entertainment.","title":"Moon Hee-joon","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moon_Hee-joon"}},"Q489432":{"id":"Q489432","name":"Luna","ko":"루나","birthName":"박선영","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Park Sun-young"],"birth":"1993-08-12","death":"","birth